@cc [label:rule] stdlib-only
ncm.ts imports node builtins only. a runtime dependency MUST NOT be added to the checker.
deletes: an install step, a lockfile entry, and a supply-chain read for the checker.

@cc [label:rule] language-agnostic
the checker reads @cc blocks out of comment text. it MUST NOT parse a language's syntax tree.
deletes: per-language extractors; code-contracts ships 2,297 lines of them for four languages.

@cc [label:rule] git-scoped
file discovery is `git grep --untracked` for `@cc` over tracked and untracked-unignored files. there is no directory walker and no per-file sniff.
deletes: skip-lists for node_modules, build output, and scratch checkouts, and the binary sniff.

@cc [label:rule] two-labels
a contract's label is `rule` or `ceiling`. any other label, or none, is a finding.
deletes: owner and notify handling and the review-bot vocabulary behind them.

@cc [label:rule] trailer-required
a rule ends with `deletes:` and a ceiling ends with `until:`. the checker enforces both.
deletes: the model-judged question "does this contract earn its place"; it is now a grep.

@cc [label:rule] budget-twelve
a CONTRACTS file holds at most 12 contracts.
deletes: discovery tooling for rules; a 12-entry file is read whole on entering the repo.

@cc [label:rule] one-skill
the plugin ships one skill. audit, verification, and the ledger are its scope arguments.
deletes: separate audit, debt, and verify skills and their overlapping descriptions.

@cc [label:rule] no-hooks
the plugin registers no hooks. the doctrine reaches every session and subagent through a CLAUDE.md import of doctrine.md.
deletes: SessionStart and SubagentStart injectors and their per-session token cost.
